WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.701 --> 00:00:03.267
♪♪

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:04.901
-Hey, everybody.
Welcome to "Corrections."

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:06.167
We all-in?

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:07.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:12.901 --> 00:00:15.300
I, um...

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:19.067
I told you I received a Lego guy
with an Emmy,

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:20.200
but he couldn't hold the Emmy,

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.067
which I thought
was part of the joke.

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:25.434
A bunch of the Lego enthusiasts
who watch this show

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:28.968
told me exactly
how he could hold it.

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:33.133
So that's how it looks.
Thank you, psychos.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:39.634
Um, last week
on "A Closer Look,"

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:43.267
we talked about goldfish
at Mar-a-Lago.

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:46.400
We said Mar-a-Lago
looked like a...

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.834
castle you put
in a goldfish bowl.

00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:50.000
That was the photo we used.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.868
A bunch of you said
those aren't goldfish.

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:56.534
In our defense, they are
very hard fish to find.

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:58.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.501
The rarest.

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:05.601
It would be like
if someone said,

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:09.167
"I'll take a turkey sandwich."

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:12.801
This short notice?

00:01:12.801 --> 00:01:14.701
W-Where in the city?!

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.767
The parts at IKEA
don't have weird names --

00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:23.267
just the finished product.

00:01:23.267 --> 00:01:25.667
They use numbers or letters

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:27.767
so that they can work
internationally --

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:29.634
numbers like "Klurgentop."

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:31.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:33.334
Letters like "Shyorlnd."

00:01:35.934 --> 00:01:38.367
We made a joke about
somebody getting caught twice

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:39.501
on "To Catch a Predator."

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:41.133
Same dude.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:43.033
Turns out that happened.

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:46.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:49.167
And I guess...
the dude wanted it to happen.

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:51.534
You always hear pedophiles
have a very hard time in prison.

00:01:51.534 --> 00:01:54.000
They're treated very badly.
Justifiably so.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.968
But I guess if you are a
pedophile who gets caught twice,

00:01:56.968 --> 00:02:00.133
it's like a double negative.

00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:01.834
King of the cellblock.

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:07.367
I'm not gonna criticize
prison rules.

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:10.834
I referred to a sobriety test
as a drunk-driving test.

00:02:10.834 --> 00:02:14.334
Obviously, it's called
a sobriety test.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.234
There are still parts
of the South

00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:18.701
where they give you
a drunk-driving test,

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:22.534
and if you do well enough,
they just send you off.

00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:24.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:31.100
"Just stay on the shoulder,
Cletus!"

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:41.501
Fat Bear Week is held
in an Alaskan national park.

00:02:41.501 --> 00:02:44.868
I pronounced that park
"cat, my."

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:48.133
It's pronounced "cat, may."

00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:51.701
The bears request
you pronounce fat "big-boned."

00:02:51.701 --> 00:02:54.501
[ Man laughs ]

00:02:54.501 --> 00:02:56.167
Oh, thank you, Bucky.

00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:57.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:03.033
"I went down
to the Five and Dime, Bucky,

00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:04.934
and I told 'em
my fat-bear joke,

00:03:04.934 --> 00:03:07.501
and not a smile!

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:11.334
But I knew
you'd like it, Bucky.

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:12.634
I told 'em, and I'm like,

00:03:12.634 --> 00:03:15.567
'You aren't
cracking a smile, now.'"

00:03:15.567 --> 00:03:17.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:20.267
"My Bucky.
When my Bucky hears my jokes,

00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:21.767
he slaps his knee so hard,

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:23.901
we're gonna have to
have it replaced!"

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:25.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.534 --> 00:03:37.901
We talked about Donald Trump

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:41.167
referring to a gorilla
in the Bronx Zoo as Mongo.

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:43.801
There is not a gorilla
in the Bronx Zoo named Mongo.

00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:46.033
There is one named Ernie,
and someone said,

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:48.701
"Do yourself a favor
and look at the picture of Ernie

00:03:48.701 --> 00:03:50.667
they have on the website."

00:03:50.667 --> 00:03:53.400
And I thought, what could
possibly be worth it?

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.434
And the answer is...this.

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:57.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.634 --> 00:04:03.400
This is what Ernie
would look like

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:07.100
if he also was arrested
on January 6th.

00:04:11.634 --> 00:04:15.367
Monday's "Closer Look,"
we had a joke about Scrabble

00:04:15.367 --> 00:04:18.767
and we showed a bunch
of Scrabble pieces.

00:04:18.767 --> 00:04:21.267
This is what we showed.
Okay? That was in the key.

00:04:21.267 --> 00:04:24.734
The key is the little square
over my shoulder, right?

00:04:24.734 --> 00:04:26.634
Someone wrote,
"Not only is the Q missing

00:04:26.634 --> 00:04:29.601
from the Scrabble game,
but you have an extra X,

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:31.367
where Scrabble games
only have one X tile.

00:04:31.367 --> 00:04:34.300
Also, there are four S tiles,
not six as shown."

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.834
My question to you is,
how big is your [bleep] TV?

00:04:36.834 --> 00:04:38.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:44.934
This was a very good graphic
that I should have

00:04:44.934 --> 00:04:47.033
given more credit
to the graphics department for

00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:50.701
about someone smoking weed
out of a CVS receipt.

00:04:50.701 --> 00:04:55.868
And I was told receipts
come from thermal printers,

00:04:55.868 --> 00:04:58.033
which use BPA in the paper.

00:04:58.033 --> 00:04:59.367
That is a chemical.

00:04:59.367 --> 00:05:02.400
BPA is a chemical called
bisphenol,

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.868
which is an endocrine disruptor.

00:05:04.868 --> 00:05:06.701
They should not be smoked
because they contain

00:05:06.701 --> 00:05:08.901
carbon and graphite.

00:05:08.901 --> 00:05:11.067
They're very dangerous.

00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:13.634
But isn't danger
a little bit of the fun?

00:05:13.634 --> 00:05:15.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.133 --> 00:05:20.701
Scollins wrote a joke

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:24.167
about dead bodies
in McDonald ball pits.

00:05:24.167 --> 00:05:27.167
I was told there haven't been
PlayPlaces in McDonald's

00:05:27.167 --> 00:05:29.901
since at least 2010.

00:05:29.901 --> 00:05:32.167
They shut them down
because they were crime scenes.

00:05:36.734 --> 00:05:40.868
I said there were not ushers
at football games.

00:05:40.868 --> 00:05:43.434
I was told by a lot of people

00:05:43.434 --> 00:05:45.701
there are ushers
at football games.

00:05:45.701 --> 00:05:49.801
In my defense, they just take me
right to the luxury box.

00:05:49.801 --> 00:05:51.567
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:59.801
I know not of A-25, B-44.

00:05:59.801 --> 00:06:02.501
But once I sit,
I'm just like you --

00:06:02.501 --> 00:06:08.734
watching our competing squads
duke it out on the gridiron.

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:11.234
I enjoy a hot-dog sandwich

00:06:11.234 --> 00:06:15.234
as much as the next
work-a-day Joe.

00:06:15.234 --> 00:06:17.100
A nice tall glass of --

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:20.868
Shoemaker, what's that
pauper's ale you enjoy?

00:06:20.868 --> 00:06:22.200
Boodveiser.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:23.767
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:29.901
I was told -- We always --

00:06:29.901 --> 00:06:34.567
In the preface to
Surprise Inspection,

00:06:34.567 --> 00:06:37.067
we described the jokes
as unusable,

00:06:37.067 --> 00:06:39.133
and I was told by a lot
of people they are usable

00:06:39.133 --> 00:06:40.834
once you put them
in Surprise Inspection

00:06:40.834 --> 00:06:44.033
because they're on TV.

00:06:44.033 --> 00:06:45.501
Fine.

00:06:45.501 --> 00:06:46.801
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.367 --> 00:06:51.834
Um, we said Nancy Mace
looked like

00:06:51.834 --> 00:06:53.667
she was wearing
an "A" on her chest,

00:06:53.667 --> 00:06:55.400
that she looks like
she hangs out

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:59.234
by Oscar's trash can
selling drugs.

00:06:59.234 --> 00:07:01.100
And then we had her saying,
"Psst. Elmo."

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.501
People thought it was a mistake.

00:07:02.501 --> 00:07:04.400
If she was hanging out
by Oscar's trash can,

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:05.934
why wouldn't she say it
to Oscar?

00:07:05.934 --> 00:07:07.434
But you wouldn't sell
Oscar drugs

00:07:07.434 --> 00:07:09.167
because he doesn't have
the money for it.

00:07:09.167 --> 00:07:11.000
[ Laughter ]

00:07:13.934 --> 00:07:16.934
I'm very disappointed still --

00:07:16.934 --> 00:07:18.901
I feel like today's generation
doesn't know

00:07:18.901 --> 00:07:21.000
that Stevie Nicks
was the scarf lady.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:29.167
I mean, it's kind of a bummer.

00:07:29.167 --> 00:07:31.534
I feel like Johnny Depp,
like, became the scarf guy,

00:07:31.534 --> 00:07:35.767
but she's a far better,
nontoxic scarf person.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:41.734
She's, like,
the best at scarves.

00:07:41.734 --> 00:07:46.033
You hear she's opening
a new scarf place?

00:07:46.033 --> 00:07:48.667
You know what it's called?
Scarf Face.

00:07:48.667 --> 00:07:50.801
[ Laughter ]

00:07:53.033 --> 00:07:56.267
It's called Scarf Face.

00:07:56.267 --> 00:07:59.367
And I saw the commercial.

00:07:59.367 --> 00:08:02.667
She's like,
"We got big scarves...

00:08:02.667 --> 00:08:05.434
medium scarves.

00:08:05.434 --> 00:08:06.834
Say hello to my little friend."

00:08:06.834 --> 00:08:08.067
[Bleep]

00:08:08.067 --> 00:08:09.400
[ Laughter ]

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:11.701
[Bleep]
Clutched on the scarf!

00:08:16.667 --> 00:08:18.767
We were also talking about
"Silver Springs"

00:08:18.767 --> 00:08:22.434
is the greatest revenge song
of all time.

00:08:22.434 --> 00:08:24.934
Stevie Nicks writes
"Silver Springs"

00:08:24.934 --> 00:08:28.167
about Lindsey Buckingham,
and it's the best.

00:08:28.167 --> 00:08:31.200
And it's a bummer --

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.167
It was supposed
to be on "Rumours."

00:08:33.167 --> 00:08:34.667
She had the publishing to it.

00:08:34.667 --> 00:08:36.200
She gave the publishing
to her mom.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:37.868
"Rumours" is one of the
best-selling albums of all time.

00:08:37.868 --> 00:08:40.300
Lindsey Buckingham
wouldn't let it be on "Rumours."

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:42.100
She was mad about it forever.

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:44.334
And then in the late '90s,
they did a live concert.

00:08:44.334 --> 00:08:46.467
It's one of the great
live concert performances

00:08:46.467 --> 00:08:48.133
because she's singing this song,

00:08:48.133 --> 00:08:51.200
this breakup song about
Lindsey Buckingham, to him

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:54.100
while he has to
play along with it.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:56.300
And I was so bummed because
I would love to show it to you

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:59.367
as a bit of music education,
but as I established last week,

00:08:59.367 --> 00:09:01.467
we've got this music licensing
issue, right?

00:09:01.467 --> 00:09:02.667
If we show it, it can't stay up.

00:09:02.667 --> 00:09:06.868
But then one of
you legal eagles...

00:09:06.868 --> 00:09:11.100
said, "You can play a song

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:12.667
with the exception

00:09:12.667 --> 00:09:14.434
that if you're reviewing
or reacting to it,

00:09:14.434 --> 00:09:15.968
it's considered
critiquing a work,

00:09:15.968 --> 00:09:17.267
which is covered under fair use,

00:09:17.267 --> 00:09:19.434
and thus means YouTube
would not take it down.

00:09:19.434 --> 00:09:21.267
So as long as you play
the music clip

00:09:21.267 --> 00:09:25.267
and then give an opinion on it,
you should be covered."

00:09:25.267 --> 00:09:26.734
So this is a clip

00:09:26.734 --> 00:09:28.400
of Stevie Nicks
and Lindsey Buckingham.

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:30.067
If you want to know
which one is which,

00:09:30.067 --> 00:09:33.334
Stevie Nicks is the one
with the scarves.

00:09:33.334 --> 00:09:34.534
Take a look.

00:09:34.534 --> 00:09:36.934
♪ I'll follow you down ♪

00:09:36.934 --> 00:09:39.701
♪ Till the sound of my voice ♪

00:09:39.701 --> 00:09:41.767
♪ Will haunt you ♪

00:09:41.767 --> 00:09:43.167
♪♪

00:09:43.167 --> 00:09:45.400
♪ Give me just a chance ♪

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:49.100
♪ You will never get away,
never get away ♪

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:51.567
♪ From the sound of the woman
that loves you ♪

00:09:51.567 --> 00:09:53.834
-♪ Never get away ♪

00:09:53.834 --> 00:09:57.868
♪♪

00:09:57.868 --> 00:09:59.968
And my opinion is,
that's [bleep] rad.

00:09:59.968 --> 00:10:01.601
So we good.

00:10:01.601 --> 00:10:03.434
[ Laughter ]

00:10:07.901 --> 00:10:13.367
I said that "Edge of Seventeen"
is a Baba O'Riley situation,

00:10:13.367 --> 00:10:15.033
which is
you should be calling it

00:10:15.033 --> 00:10:16.601
the thing we all think it is.

00:10:16.601 --> 00:10:18.834
In its defense, at least,
"Edge of Seventeen"

00:10:18.834 --> 00:10:20.934
is in white-winged Doug --

00:10:20.934 --> 00:10:22.234
White-winged Doug?

00:10:22.234 --> 00:10:24.267
[ Laughter ]

00:10:27.934 --> 00:10:31.000
But there's no -- "Baba O'Riley"
does not appear --

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:33.701
The words "Baba O'Riley" do not
appear in "Teenage Wasteland."

00:10:33.701 --> 00:10:36.501
Another -- You gave me some
good other examples of that.

00:10:36.501 --> 00:10:38.234
"Good Riddance"
is the Green Day song

00:10:38.234 --> 00:10:42.467
that should be called
"Time of Your Life."

00:10:42.467 --> 00:10:44.901
"For What It's Worth"
is a Buffalo Springfield song

00:10:44.901 --> 00:10:47.701
that never mentions
"For what it's worth."

00:10:47.701 --> 00:10:49.767
The Who did this a lot.

00:10:49.767 --> 00:10:52.267
Obviously, "Baba O'Riley" should
be called "Teenage Wasteland."

00:10:52.267 --> 00:10:55.367
The song that you think
should be called
"Won't Get Fooled Again"

00:10:55.367 --> 00:10:57.200
is called "Jeff McIntyre."

00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:59.000
[ Laughter ]

00:11:02.701 --> 00:11:04.033
Alright.

00:11:06.634 --> 00:11:08.000
Scollins did this.

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.734
We all remember Scollins
wore a tank top, right?

00:11:10.734 --> 00:11:14.901
Then, uh,
got some art sent to us

00:11:14.901 --> 00:11:17.701
by a wonderful artist
named T.J.

00:11:17.701 --> 00:11:19.968
He sent that. It was great.

00:11:19.968 --> 00:11:22.667
Then, the other day, I'm in
the audience doing the Q&amp;A,

00:11:22.667 --> 00:11:27.000
and I notice a guy wearing
the Scollins tank-top art.

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:31.701
I ask, and it is the dude
who drew it. Came to our show.

00:11:31.701 --> 00:11:33.667
And so Scollins
posted this photo,

00:11:33.667 --> 00:11:35.467
and all the comments
were like,

00:11:35.467 --> 00:11:38.234
"Whoa, that dude's
so [bleep] hot."

00:11:38.234 --> 00:11:40.834
And Scollins and I want to know
when you say "that dude,"

00:11:40.834 --> 00:11:43.534
do you mean me
or the Scollins in the drawing?

00:11:43.534 --> 00:11:45.367
[ Laughter ]

00:11:50.567 --> 00:11:52.501
We're of two minds.

00:11:56.934 --> 00:11:59.000
♪ Doo-doo-doo-doo ♪

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:01.701
Someone wrote a comment
that I really enjoyed this week.

00:12:01.701 --> 00:12:04.133
"When I watch 'Corrections,'
I don't know what's happening."

00:12:04.133 --> 00:12:06.067
[ Laughter ]

00:12:08.167 --> 00:12:09.734
That's the goal.
That's how this is different.

00:12:09.734 --> 00:12:14.334
We're not the normal pablum
you're fed.

00:12:14.334 --> 00:12:16.000
We're challenging you.

00:12:17.801 --> 00:12:19.601
Speaking of challenging,
last week,

00:12:19.601 --> 00:12:23.901
I tried to do three
noncontiguous fingers

00:12:23.901 --> 00:12:29.234
to show how Ron DeSantis
eats pudding,

00:12:29.234 --> 00:12:32.367
and it did take me longer
than I thought it would take.

00:12:32.367 --> 00:12:35.300
And someone said, "Why does it
take him that long to do it?"

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:37.334
Interestingly enough,

00:12:37.334 --> 00:12:40.934
doing three
noncontiguous fingers

00:12:40.934 --> 00:12:43.767
is considered
a drunk-driving test.

00:12:43.767 --> 00:12:46.934
[ Laughter ]

00:12:46.934 --> 00:12:48.267
Heh.

00:12:49.534 --> 00:12:52.100
Um, someone said it is --

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:54.534
This is a Jackal
Joke of the Week.

00:12:56.601 --> 00:12:59.801
Someone said, "Negroni
is a good drink for this

00:12:59.801 --> 00:13:03.334
because when I hear your jokes,
I'm at home ne-groaning."

00:13:07.133 --> 00:13:09.167
So congrats on the win.

00:13:09.167 --> 00:13:12.667
[ Laughter ]

00:13:12.667 --> 00:13:15.868
I got some bad news, though.
Want to see the trophy?

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:26.400
Um, the gentleman who made these
reached out.

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:28.934
He was angry because --
He wanted to make it clear.

00:13:28.934 --> 00:13:31.634
These are called head jackals.

00:13:31.634 --> 00:13:33.801
He also was upset

00:13:33.801 --> 00:13:38.534
because he attached a video
of how they're made.

00:13:38.534 --> 00:13:40.868
Uh, and he wanted me
to show them to people.

00:13:40.868 --> 00:13:44.767
I don't know if you want
to see how they're made.

00:13:44.767 --> 00:13:46.968
What happens is, like,

00:13:46.968 --> 00:13:49.367
a mommy one of these
and a daddy one of these...

00:13:49.367 --> 00:13:50.767
[ Laughter ]

00:13:55.834 --> 00:13:57.934
I said it's "patented."

00:13:57.934 --> 00:14:01.434
Someone said, "When it's art,
it's a copyright, not patent."

00:14:03.868 --> 00:14:05.300
"Art."

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:07.100
[ Laughter ]

00:14:08.968 --> 00:14:11.267
I do -- Let's see what else. Oh!

00:14:11.267 --> 00:14:13.767
You know, I think
a lot of people thought...

00:14:16.601 --> 00:14:18.501
Oh, people have been
criticizing my nails

00:14:18.501 --> 00:14:19.934
and saying I need a manicure.

00:14:19.934 --> 00:14:21.667
I'm gonna try not --

00:14:21.667 --> 00:14:23.734
I'm not gonna show them to you.

00:14:23.734 --> 00:14:25.467
I'm gonna try to get my nails
in good shape,

00:14:25.467 --> 00:14:26.934
because then I am
gonna show you --

00:14:26.934 --> 00:14:29.100
I'm gonna make
these jackals hump,

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:31.300
but I'm gonna wait
until my fingers

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:33.834
are pretty enough for it.

00:14:33.834 --> 00:14:36.634
A lot of people thought
I was faking

00:14:36.634 --> 00:14:40.434
Scollins and Wally coming in.

00:14:40.434 --> 00:14:43.334
Uh, well, guess what.

00:14:43.334 --> 00:14:49.000
We got some Zapruder footage
for ya. Roll it, Alex.

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:52.033
I want to start by saying,
if you can sense a vibe --

00:14:52.033 --> 00:14:54.534
Are you [bleep] kidding me?

00:14:54.534 --> 00:14:56.167
[ Laughter ]

00:14:56.167 --> 00:14:58.734
Wally and Scollins come in
chatting it up.

00:14:58.734 --> 00:15:02.467
[ Laughter ]

00:15:02.467 --> 00:15:04.334
During "Corrections."

00:15:04.334 --> 00:15:06.834
[ Laughter ]

00:15:06.834 --> 00:15:09.234
Is nothing sacred in this place?

00:15:11.734 --> 00:15:13.968
[ Smooching ]

00:15:18.734 --> 00:15:20.701
"Should we? Oh, I don't know."

00:15:20.701 --> 00:15:24.334
[ Smooching ]

00:15:24.334 --> 00:15:28.133
"What if...
What if someone sees us?"

00:15:28.133 --> 00:15:29.634
"No one's watching."

00:15:29.634 --> 00:15:31.367
[ Smooching ]

00:15:42.534 --> 00:15:45.601
[ Laughter ]

00:15:45.601 --> 00:15:49.601
[ Ominous violin screeching ]

00:15:56.501 --> 00:15:58.501
Would you guys believe
we don't rehearse?

00:15:58.501 --> 00:16:02.234
[ Laughter ]

00:16:02.234 --> 00:16:05.434
First time we ever did that.

00:16:05.434 --> 00:16:07.801
Stevie Nicks week.
[see ya next week]

